---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';

const example = `match local.clock.compare(&remote.clock) {
    Order::Before => MergeDecision::UseRemote,
    Order::After => MergeDecision::KeepLocal,
    Order::Concurrent => MergeDecision::Conflict,
    Order::Equal if local.value == remote.value => MergeDecision::Same,
    Order::Equal => MergeDecision::Conflict,
}`;
---
<Base lang="en" title="Local sync Rust sample | Miguel" description="Independent Rust example with vector clocks, conflict detection and an acknowledged outbox.">
  <main id="contenido" class="detail-main wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/lab/">← Back to the lab</a>
    <div class="detail-hero"><div><p class="section-kicker">LAB / RUST</p><h1 class="long-title">Local changes<span>.</span></h1><p class="detail-lede">A small example of causal versus concurrent changes and retrying pending operations.</p></div><div class="detail-badge">RUST / STD<br /><strong>INDEPENDENT SAMPLE</strong></div></div>
    <div class="detail-meta"><div><span>CAUSALITY</span><strong>Vector clocks</strong></div><div><span>DELIVERY</span><strong>Acknowledged outbox</strong></div><div><span>VERIFIED</span><strong>5 local tests</strong></div></div>
    <div class="case-layout"><aside><span>01 / PROBLEM</span><span>02 / DECISION</span><span>03 / CODE</span><span>04 / LIMITS</span></aside><div class="case-content">
      <section><p class="section-kicker">01 / PROBLEM</p><h2>Two devices can edit the same record.</h2><p>When both work offline, a timestamp cannot show whether one change had observed the other. The sample uses per actor counters to identify causal order and concurrency.</p></section>
      <section><p class="section-kicker">02 / DECISION</p><h2>Detect before resolving.</h2><p>A causally newer clock can win. Concurrent clocks produce an explicit conflict for product rules to resolve. Outgoing operations remain pending until acknowledged.</p></section>
      <section><p class="section-kicker">03 / CODE</p><h2>The comparison is explicit.</h2><pre class="sample-code"><code>{example}</code></pre><p>The full code and tests are in <code>samples/local-sync-rust</code> inside this independent portfolio repository. Miguel should review and explain the sample before using it as professional evidence.</p></section>
      <section><p class="section-kicker">04 / LIMITS</p><h2>A sample, not a production engine.</h2><p>It has no durable persistence, transport, authentication, encryption or automatic conflict policy. It contains no private Meson code.</p></section>
    </div></div>
